.TH ETE 1 "October 2026" "ETE 1.0.4-octa" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ete \- ECHO terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ete
.RI [ +LINE ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B ete
.BR --version
.br
.B ete
.BR --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ete
is a full-screen terminal text editor with syntax highlighting, line numbers,
mouse support, undo and redo, find and replace, automatic indentation, and
word wrap. It uses Python 3 and the standard library.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI + LINE
Open the file with the cursor on the specified line. This argument may appear
before or after the file name.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed version and exit. The short form is
.BR -v .
.TP
.B --help
Print command-line help and exit. The short form is
.BR -h .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE
The file to open or create. If omitted, start with an empty buffer.
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
Run
.B ete
in an interactive terminal. Press F1 inside the editor for the keyboard
shortcut reference. Ctrl+Q quits; unsaved changes prompt for confirmation.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.8 or newer and a compatible curses-enabled terminal.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/ShadyDevelopment/ECHO-Text-Editor/issues
the project issue tracker.
.UE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
